WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.280
- Our next guest is a very funny woman

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.520
that you've seen in HBO's "Insecure."

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.700
she's got a book out now,

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.750
it's called "Bamboozled by Jesus:

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.009
How God Tricked Me Into
the Life of My Dreams.

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:11.390
(laughing)
The best title.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:14.027
Please, everybody welcome ,Yvonne Orji!

00:00:14.027 --> 00:00:14.860
(clapping)

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:18.840
(audience cheering)
(upbeat pop music)

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.590
- I did this for you!

00:00:26.514 --> 00:00:30.630
- Gosh, you look- this
might be my favorite outfit

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.896
that anyone's ever worn.

00:00:31.896 --> 00:00:34.770
The hair, the earrings,
the lipstick, oh my God.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:35.603
- It's a thing.

00:00:35.603 --> 00:00:36.522
- You look fabulous!

00:00:36.522 --> 00:00:38.810
- I did it for you, ma'am!

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:39.643
- Oh my God.

00:00:39.643 --> 00:00:41.320
- I kind of match the color scheme.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.742
- Yes, you're so colorful, I love it.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:43.700
- Thank you.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:44.533
- Oh my God. Yeah you just walked out

00:00:44.533 --> 00:00:46.057
and I'm just jealous.

00:00:46.057 --> 00:00:47.850
It's nice to meet you!

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.470
- It's a- I am a huge fan.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.450
- Oh- even if you're lying- thank you.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.330
- No, ut I'm not, though because I had the

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:57.430
Miseducation of Lauren
Hill room with the karaoke

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:59.440
background, I may or may
not have been jamming out

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.929
to (sings) since you've been gone!

00:01:00.929 --> 00:01:01.762
(laughter)

00:01:01.762 --> 00:01:03.124
- And I am not a singer whatsoever.

00:01:03.124 --> 00:01:04.760
- You should've put on her record.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:05.690
That's like one of my favorites.

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:06.680
That's why it's that room.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:07.580
- That's why it's that room?

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.530
- Yeah, those are all
like my favorite records-

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:11.260
- Oh I saw the Alanis
Morrissette "Jagged Little Pill"

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:12.093
- Yes.

00:01:12.093 --> 00:01:12.926
- Oh that was-

00:01:12.926 --> 00:01:14.110
- I got some Annie Lennox
in there, so yeah, yeah.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:15.987
- Remember those Columbia House stickers?

00:01:15.987 --> 00:01:16.820
- Yes.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.740
- That was- so Columbia House was a thing

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:21.193
you could mail stickers and
they would send you CDs.

00:01:21.193 --> 00:01:22.026
(laughter)

00:01:22.026 --> 00:01:22.859
- And you would get CDs.

00:01:22.859 --> 00:01:23.692
- Google it.

00:01:23.692 --> 00:01:24.525
- So CDs were um-

00:01:24.525 --> 00:01:25.358
(laughter)

00:01:25.358 --> 00:01:28.359
- Alanis Morissette was one
of my first CDs I ever got.

00:01:28.359 --> 00:01:29.192
- Me too.

00:01:29.192 --> 00:01:30.420
- Oh my gosh, Jagged
Little Pill, so classic.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.220
- I was like "she's saying
it all, and I'm in."

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.053
- Yes.

00:01:33.053 --> 00:01:33.886
- Yes.

00:01:33.886 --> 00:01:35.992
- But I'm only allowed to
sing songs where I yell,

00:01:35.992 --> 00:01:38.750
cause I don't sing,
because if I could sing,

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:39.627
I would be a stripper.

00:01:39.627 --> 00:01:42.216
(laughter)

00:01:42.216 --> 00:01:44.830
- Did you say "if I could
sing id be a stripper"?

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:46.500
- God could not trust
me with a singing voice,

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.350
like He knows ho He can trust,

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.397
because I would be that
person like "how you doing?"

00:01:51.397 --> 00:01:55.517
"yeah yeah. Drop it low"

00:01:55.517 --> 00:01:57.328
"Chocolate Testimony"
would be my stripper name.

00:01:57.328 --> 00:01:59.270
- "Chocolate Testimony"?

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:00.690
- I had the whole thing planned out,

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:01.810
but that's why God was like-

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:05.200
- You have got to make that show. (laughs)

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.641
- He keeps me humble. Like
two things I cannot have-

00:02:07.641 --> 00:02:09.510
I can't have 6 pack abs, cause, again,

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.035
I would wear pasties to
church and I just don't think

00:02:11.035 --> 00:02:11.868
that that's appropriate.

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:13.263
- I think that God would frown.

00:02:13.263 --> 00:02:15.919
- I think He'd be like
"Daughter, what are we doing?"

00:02:15.919 --> 00:02:18.610
So He keeps me humble
with like a humble pouch

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:19.670
and like a (clicks).

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:20.785
- I always say that about Salma Hayak.

00:02:20.785 --> 00:02:22.447
I was like, when I'd
see Salma Hayak I'm like

00:02:22.447 --> 00:02:24.183
"God didn't allow me to look
that good for a reason."

00:02:24.183 --> 00:02:26.880
I would be just walking around naked.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.200
Yup, she's so beautiful.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.350
- You have to know your limitations
and He knew them before.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:32.183
- He knew.

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:35.182
- He knew. Girl, please.

00:02:35.182 --> 00:02:38.235
- You are so funny. Wait but
before you got "Insecure"

00:02:38.235 --> 00:02:41.170
on HBO, I heard that you
were a wedding emcee,

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:42.400
which is awesome.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.450
- Yes. I was the ultimate
hype woman at every event.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.720
I did weddings, birthdays, baby showers.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:48.770
- Your personality is perfect for it.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:51.024
- Bless you, hello. Are we best friends

00:02:51.024 --> 00:02:54.078
because all this love that
you're giving me right now

00:02:54.078 --> 00:02:57.210
like I'm a sunflower, I'm
blooming, I'm in full bloom.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.043
- Full bloom.

00:02:58.043 --> 00:02:58.876
- Yes.

00:02:58.876 --> 00:03:00.013
- What was it like, though?

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:00.846
- (exhales)

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:01.880
- Because brides can be crazy.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:04.300
- Well, it's not really so much
the brides. The bridesmaids.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.133
- Oh, really?

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:09.160
- Girl. Hosting weddings kind
of turned me off to weddings

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:12.180
for a long time because you
see how the sausage is made.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:13.729
So, yes the brides can
be a little bit like

00:03:13.729 --> 00:03:14.754
"This is what I want"

00:03:14.754 --> 00:03:17.521
but then the bridesmaids
sometimes are a little like

00:03:17.521 --> 00:03:19.770
low-key haters. Like they are!

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:20.603
- On the bride?

00:03:20.603 --> 00:03:21.886
- Because it's not their day,

00:03:21.886 --> 00:03:23.922
like especially the single
ones, like it's not their day.

00:03:23.922 --> 00:03:26.290
So it's like "oh, but I want to do this"

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:27.950
it's like "boo boo, I
just need you to line up

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:30.517
and walk out when I say
walk. Like real talk,

00:03:30.517 --> 00:03:33.781
I just don't any lip.
Just follow me, here!"

00:03:33.781 --> 00:03:35.720
And I'm just like "You're
not paying my check.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:38.360
You're not cutting my check
so just do what I say."

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.193
- Just get in the line.

00:03:39.193 --> 00:03:41.050
- "I got orders from the
woman in white, okay?"

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:43.864
- Oh my God. (laughs) That's horrible.

00:03:43.864 --> 00:03:45.240
Having bridesmaids like that.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.900
- Sometimes I want to
send a thank you note,

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:49.664
like "thank you for having
me to host your wedding,

00:03:49.664 --> 00:03:51.377
also, check your friends, girl."

00:03:51.377 --> 00:03:53.650
- "Also, the redhead? Don't trust her."

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:56.542
- "Also, everybody's not for you."

00:03:56.542 --> 00:03:58.487
- "Every friendship has a season."

00:03:58.487 --> 00:04:01.437
- "And this one has come to an end."

00:04:01.437 --> 00:04:02.737
- But I want to talk about your new book,

00:04:02.737 --> 00:04:04.437
it's called "Bamboozled by Jesus"

00:04:04.437 --> 00:04:07.160
so why is it called that?
It's an amazing title.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:09.723
- Because girl, first of
all, the fact that I am

00:04:09.723 --> 00:04:11.811
sitting on this couch, this
is a big bamboozling moment

00:04:11.811 --> 00:04:15.085
because I was supposed to
be a doctor, I really was.

00:04:15.085 --> 00:04:18.053
My last name is "Orji" so
that wasn't gonna work.

00:04:19.897 --> 00:04:22.217
"Paging Dr. Orji to gynecology"?

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:26.700
I was like that's a set
up. Stop playing. Stop it.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.970
And I also don't like blood
so I don't know how this

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:30.210
is gonna work out.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:31.410
- I love you so much.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:34.400
- And so, but I didn't
know what else to do,

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:38.128
so I literally was doing the thing.

00:04:38.128 --> 00:04:41.364
I went to college, I
have a degree in biology,

00:04:41.364 --> 00:04:44.140
and all of the things, and
then, when I was getting

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:46.760
my master's in public
health, I entered a pageant

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.394
and God told me to do
comedy, and I was like

00:04:48.394 --> 00:04:50.060
"Mm, You don't know."

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.364
Because I was like "that
makes no sense. I'm not funny.

00:04:52.364 --> 00:04:53.567
I've never done stand-up."

00:04:53.567 --> 00:04:56.060
- You're one of the
funniest people who has ever

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.135
been in my presence.
I'm so happy right now.

00:04:58.135 --> 00:05:01.670
- Thank you! But I
didn't know that in 2006.

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:04.440
I literally was just trying to figure out

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.640
how not to be a doctor
and how not to get out of

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:07.950
my parents' will, you know what I mean?

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:10.070
Like, this is how much I
was so afraid to tell them

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:11.450
that I didn't want to go to med school.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:12.283
- Oh no.

00:05:12.283 --> 00:05:14.887
- I got a master's degree
and then I went to live

00:05:14.887 --> 00:05:19.226
in war-torn Liberia, yes,
because I was just evading

00:05:19.226 --> 00:05:22.847
the reality of "I don't
want to do this thing that

00:05:22.847 --> 00:05:24.760
you guys really thought I would do."

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.770
- I think it's amazing that
you're writing this though,

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:28.478
and people will be able to
relate and you're hilarious.

00:05:28.478 --> 00:05:29.311
- Thank you.

00:05:29.311 --> 00:05:31.050
- You're like such a
light, and you're so funny,

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:32.820
and you've just completely
turned my mood around.

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:33.653
You're just so funny.

00:05:33.653 --> 00:05:35.079
- You're awesome! But
that was the whole thing,

00:05:35.079 --> 00:05:37.990
I wanted to write a book where
you could have faith and fun.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:39.616
Because people, especially
in Hollywood, they're like

00:05:39.616 --> 00:05:42.196
"How are you able to be
successful in Hollywood

00:05:42.196 --> 00:05:43.316
and still love Jesus?"

00:05:43.316 --> 00:05:44.980
I was like "I didn't
know I had to choose."

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:47.350
Like when did- I didn't
know it was a platter

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:49.220
- My Jesus is fun as
hell. Oh, that's funny.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:50.053
Ironic. "fun as hell"

00:05:50.053 --> 00:05:51.610
(laughter)

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:52.780
- I was like "It's a buffet"

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:56.250
so I crack jokes in the book,
I talk about my love for

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:59.697
Cardi B and DMX, and my love
for Luke 5:25, you know?

00:05:59.697 --> 00:06:02.435
Whatever! All things
work together for good.

00:06:02.435 --> 00:06:03.459
You like what I did there?

00:06:03.459 --> 00:06:05.709
(laughter)

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.840
- That was awesome. I love
that, though. I think it's

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.610
an important message, too,
and not everybody's saying it.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:11.443
I think that's really important.

00:06:11.443 --> 00:06:14.726
Everybody, Yvonne's book is
called "Bamboozled by Jesus"

00:06:14.726 --> 00:06:16.687
it's out now. You gotta check it out.

